<article class="env-lemma" id="05K1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05K1">Lemma <span data-tag="05K1">38.16.7</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of schemes of finite type over a scheme $S$. Let $s \in S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type, quasi-coherent sheaf on $Z$. Then $\mathcal{F}$ is (universally) pure along $Z_ s$ if and only if $i_*\mathcal{F}$ is (universally) pure along $X_ s$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CUD" data-tag="0CUD">31.8.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>